[1] user: Implement Gitea Issue #863: `test(backend): increase high-impact backend coverage to 75%+`.

Repository: Sport-Analytics-Tool
Authoritative repository/workflow: Gitea.
The GitHub repository is only a mirror. Do NOT push, open a PR against, or commit directly to the GitHub mirror.

Before changing anything:

1. Read and follow all applicable repository/project guidance, including:
   - `AGENTS.md`
   - `AGENTS.override.md` if present
   - Git methodology
   - project methodology
   - testing/coverage documentation
   - AI policy and AI evidence guidance
   - backend-specific README/guidance
   - relevant documentation under `docs/`
2. Inspect Gitea Issue #863 and treat its acceptance criteria as authoritative.
3. Check the current working tree and branch.
4. Fetch the latest authoritative `origin/main`.
5. Create/work on:
   `test/863-backend-high-impact-coverage`
6. Ensure the branch starts from the latest `origin/main`.

Do not use the GitHub mirror as the authoritative remote.

## Objective

Increase backend direct automated test coverage from the current baseline of roughly:

- Lines: 60.85%
- Statements: 60.02%
- Functions: 65.00%
- Branches: 52.03%

to at least:

**Backend line coverage >= 75%**

The repository-wide coverage before this issue was approximately:

- Lines: 71.45%
- Statements: 70.23%
- Functions: 76.00%
- Branches: 65.10%

However, first establish the CURRENT baseline from the latest `main`.
Do not assume these historical values are still exact.

The goal is not simply to execute uncovered lines. Add meaningful behavioural tests
around important backend code that currently has little or no direct coverage.

## Critical constraints

Do NOT reach the target by:

- adding coverage exclusions;
- narrowing `coverage.include`;
- excluding difficult repository files;
- using `istanbul ignore`, `c8 ignore`, or similar directives;
- exporting private helpers purely for testing;
- restructuring production code purely to reduce the denominator;
- deleting production code solely to improve coverage;
- weakening existing assertions;
- increasing test timeouts merely to conceal slow/broken tests;
- writing tests that only assert "does not throw";
- writing tests whose only purpose is executing lines;
- snapshotting huge SQL strings when meaningful semantic assertions are possible.

Production behaviour should remain unchanged unless a genuine defect is discovered.

If a genuine unrelated defect is found:
- identify it explicitly;
- do not silently fold a behavioural change into #863;
- recommend a separate bug issue unless the smallest possible fix is genuinely
  required for #863.

## Stage 1 — establish current baseline

Before writing tests, run:

`npm run test:coverage --workspace=@sport-analytics/backend`

Record:

- Lines
- Statements
- Functions
- Branches

Inspect:

`coverage/backend/index.html`

and/or the JSON coverage summary.

Determine the largest files with the highest number of meaningful uncovered lines.

Also run the existing backend tests without changing anything so there is a clean
pre-change baseline.

Do not blindly follow the historical percentages below if the current coverage report
has changed.

## Historical high-impact gaps

The previous coverage report showed these important gaps.

### Priority 0

#### Batch repository

`apps/backend/src/modules/batches/batch.repository.ts`

Historical line coverage: approximately 1.13%.

This is expected to be one of the highest-impact targets because it is both large and
central to the batch ingestion/review/publication workflow.

Inspect every exported/public repository operation before deciding what tests are
needed.

Cover meaningful behaviours such as those actually implemented by the repository,
including where applicable:

- batch creation;
- batch lookup;
- owner/submitter scope;
- batch state transitions;
- validation state;
- reviewer-actionable state;
- review task retrieval;
- reference-resolution persistence;
- resolution <truncated omitted_approx_tokens="2785" />dav-sundy.csv`

for this AI-assisted implementation if Nadav is the developer performing the work.

Record truthfully:

- tool;
- actual model;
- purpose;
- Issue #863;
- work performed;
- verification/adaptation;
- transcript/evidence reference where actually available.

Do not invent a transcript path if no transcript has yet been exported.

AI-assisted commits must include the appropriate trailer using the ACTUAL Codex model
used for implementation.

## Acceptance Criteria

Do not declare #863 complete unless all applicable criteria are satisfied:

- [ ] Current backend baseline was measured before changes.
- [ ] Backend line coverage reaches **>=75%**.
- [ ] Repository-wide line coverage increases materially from its current baseline.
- [ ] `batch.repository.ts` receives substantial meaningful direct coverage.
- [ ] `submission.repository.ts` receives substantial meaningful direct coverage.
- [ ] At least three additional high-impact under-covered backend modules receive
      meaningful direct coverage.
- [ ] Important success paths are tested.
- [ ] Important failure/not-found/conflict paths are tested.
- [ ] Pagination/bounds are tested where applicable.
- [ ] Ownership/scope behaviour is tested where applicable.
- [ ] Idempotent/retry behaviour is tested where applicable.
- [ ] Tests contain meaningful behavioural assertions.
- [ ] No coverage exclusions were added.
- [ ] No coverage ignore directives were added.
- [ ] No denominator manipulation occurred.
- [ ] No production restructuring occurred solely for coverage.
- [ ] Existing backend behaviour is preserved unless a separately identified defect
      requires correction.
- [ ] Backend coverage command passes.
- [ ] Repository-wide coverage command passes.
- [ ] `npm run check` passes.
- [ ] `npm run hygiene` passes.
- [ ] Existing improved workspace coverage does not regress due to this change.
- [ ] Evidence contains real before/after values.

## Working style

Use a coverage-guided, behaviour-first loop:

1. Measure.
2. Find the largest meaningful uncovered area.
3. Understand its real contract.
4. Add focused tests.
5. Run the focused tests.
6. Rerun backend coverage.
7. Repeat.

Do not attempt to write all tests before measuring their effect.

Prioritise business-critical behaviour over easy coverage.

## Before finishing

Review the complete diff.

Check specifically for:

- accidental production-code changes;
- debug output;
- skipped tests;
- `.only`;
- test-only exports;
- coverage ignores;
- excessive mocking;
- assertions that do not prove behaviour;
- duplicated fixtures/helpers;
- generated coverage artifacts accidentally staged;
- secrets or credentials.

Run:

`git status`
`git diff --check`
`git diff --stat`

and inspect the actual diff before proposing completion.

## Git and completion rules

Do NOT:

- merge;
- push;
- create a PR;
- close Issue #863;
- modify the GitHub mirror.

until I explicitly ask you to do so.

You may make local commits only if I explicitly authorize them.

Otherwise leave the implementation ready for review.

## Final response

When implementation is complete, give me:

1. exact files changed;
2. tests added;
3. behaviours covered;
4. baseline backend:
   - lines;
   - statements;
   - functions;
   - branches;
5. final backend:
   - lines;
   - statements;
   - functions;
   - branches;
6. baseline repository-wide coverage;
7. final repository-wide coverage;
8. the backend files with the largest coverage improvement;
9. verification commands and exact outcomes;
10. remaining important uncovered backend behaviour;
11. any defects discovered;
12. confirmation that no coverage manipulation was used;
13. whether every acceptance criterion for #863 is satisfied;
14. suggested PR title;
15. suggested commit message:

   test(backend): increase high-impact coverage above 75%

   Refs #863
   Assisted-by: Codex[ACTUAL MODEL]

Do not claim completion until the measured backend line coverage is at least 75%.

